<aside><h1 style="font-size:16px">AI-Factory</h1><p>A signed-in staff user opens the Overdue Invoices screen and sees every overdue invoice with its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue. On the same screen they can narrow the list with a customer filter and a fixed days-overdue bucket filter (7–30, 31–60, 61+), and the list reloads in place. The requirements describe only an API, so this single list screen is the smallest UI that covers the overdue-list requirements.</p><ul><li><a href="#S-1">S-1 <code>/invoices/overdue</code></a></li></ul><h3>No screen</h3><ul><li><b>REQ-1</b> The invoice reminders system shall classify an invoice as overdue, working this out on every request and never storing it, only when the invoice&#39;s status value is in the configured open-status list (which has no built-in client value and is set at deployment), its due date is not null, and the number of calendar days from its due date to today&#39;s date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7). <i>(no screen: A server-side rule for classifying an invoice as overdue, worked out on every request from configured statuses, time zone and threshold. Users see only its results, through the list on S-1.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-14</b> If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint has no valid authentication token from the existing API, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email or changing data. <i>(no screen: An API authentication rule: requests with no valid token get HTTP 401. It adds no screen or UI element. On S-1 it shows up only as the generic error state.)</i></li><li><b>REQ-19</b> If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint carries a valid, unexpired token from the existing API that does not hold the configured staff claim (claim type and value set in configuration, with no built-in client value), then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 403 without returning invoice or customer data or changing data. <i>(no screen: An API authorization rule: tokens without the configured staff claim get HTTP 403. It adds no screen or UI element. On S-1 it shows up only as the generic error state.)</i></li></ul></aside>
